# Copy to `.env` for local development only.
# Expo loads `.env` automatically via `expo start`. Variables prefixed with
# `EXPO_PUBLIC_` are inlined into the JS bundle at build time — same pattern
# as the web app's `VITE_` vars (see architecture.md §2.1).
#
# These are host URLs, not secrets — safe to ship in the client bundle.
# Do NOT put backend credentials, Supabase keys, or SMTP tokens here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development (default)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend API host with NO path suffix. The client appends `/api/v1/...`
# itself (api-design.md §6 — the `/api` prefix and `/v1` mount are fixed).
#
# Live Render backend (default for team + client testing):
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=https://td-it-solution-insurance.onrender.com
#
# Optional — only if you run the backend locally (see ../backend/README.md):
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.42:3000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging / preview builds (EAS `preview` profile)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Do NOT commit staging or production URLs in this file.
# Set the value in EAS instead — it is scoped to the `preview` environment:
#
#   eas env:create --name EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL \
#     --value "https://td-it-solution-insurance.onrender.com" \
#     --environment preview --visibility plaintext

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production store builds (EAS `production` profile)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Set in EAS, scoped to the `production` environment:
#
#   eas env:create --name EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL \
#     --value "https://td-it-solution-insurance.onrender.com" \
#     --environment production --visibility plaintext
#
# Before the first production build, confirm:
#   - The Render backend is deployed and `/api/health/ready` returns 200.
#   - Render's `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` includes your app origins (mobile apps
#     typically do not send an Origin header on native fetch — verify against
#     the live backend before relying on auth flows in a store build).
#   - You ran `eas env:list --environment production` and see the variable.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Feature flags (Release Gate A)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_CLAIMS — minimal build-time flag, NOT a general
# feature-flag system (see src/config/features.ts). The claims backend has
# not shipped, so client-facing builds must not expose the claims tab/routes
# or they 404 against a live customer.
#
# Any value other than the literal string "false" is treated as enabled, so
# local development defaults to claims visible even if you don't set this.
# Set explicitly to "false" to preview the "coming soon" gated state locally:
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_CLAIMS=true
#
# `mobile/eas.json` sets this per build profile already — "true" for
# `development`, "false" for `preview` and `production`. Don't flip preview/
# production to "true" until the claims backend (Feature 005) ships.

# EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_LOCATION_TRACKING — minimal build-time flag (INC-001),
# same pattern as EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_CLAIMS above (see
# src/config/features.ts). Gates every client entry point that can call
# expo-location (foreground permission prompt, getCurrentPositionAsync) or
# report a fix to `POST /v1/assets/:assetId/location-report` — the app-shell
# foreground reporter and the asset-detail "Enable location tracking" /
# "Update location now" buttons. The backend endpoint has its own
# server-side kill switch (503 when disabled), but that does not stop the
# client from raising an OS permission prompt with nowhere for the result
# to go, so the client must independently refuse to call expo-location at
# all when this flag is off.
#
# Any value other than the literal string "false" is treated as enabled, so
# local development defaults to location tracking available even if you
# don't set this. Set explicitly to "false" to preview the gated state
# locally:
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_LOCATION_TRACKING=true
#
# `mobile/eas.json` sets this per build profile already — "true" for
# `development`, "false" for `preview` and `production`. Don't flip preview/
# production to "true" until there is a real product surface (case/claim,
# GPS Stage 1 — see FU-A14) for the resulting location data.

# INC-001 A-12 — additional Feature 009 surfaces gated for Release Gate A
# criterion 6 (no Stage-8-bypassed surface reachable in client builds).
# Same `"false"` / default-enabled convention as claims and location above.
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_KYC=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_ALERTS=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_THEFT_REPORTING=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_HARDWARE_TRACKING=true
EXPO_PUBLIC_FEATURE_SECURITY_OPERATOR=true
#
# `mobile/eas.json` sets all of these to "false" for preview and production.
